    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1202">

                <pb facs="0851" n="735" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg735"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.512/208.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Alger to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mazatlan</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-03-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 12, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your March 11. Have no communication outside city. Understand all mining
                    companies in Sinaloa called on to pay and are paying or have paid. W. Felton, E.
                    H. Hoag and Chas. Thomas, residents Mazatlan, inform they have paid.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Alger</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
